  If you use these patterns in your systems, research, or publications,
  please cite this repository using the metadata below.
type: software
title: >-
  private-capital-agent-audit: Governance Patterns for Autonomous AI
  Agents at SEC-Registered Investment Advisers
authors:
  - family-names: Bhaduri
    given-names: Kunjar
    orcid: ""
    affiliation: North Texas Capital Investments
    website: "https://linkedin.com/in/kunjarbhaduri"
repository-code: "https://github.com/linus10x/private-capital-agent-audit"
url: "https://github.com/linus10x/private-capital-agent-audit"
abstract: >-
  Reference governance patterns for audit-ready autonomous AI agents at
  SEC-registered investment advisers (private capital). Built to the
  Investment Advisers Act fiduciary regime under §206 (duty of care +
  duty of loyalty, per SEC Release IA-5248). Ships five corrected
  Autonomy Ladder primitives — an A0–A4 level gate requiring independent
  attestation, a sovereign veto that an agent cannot self-clear, a
  deployer-keyed hash-chain ledger with witness-anchored regeneration
  resistance, a DEFCON risk-state machine with a transition-direction
  guard, and an effective-challenge harness that rejects self-validation
  — each paired with a committed adversarial probe. Adds seven
  adviser-native controls: best execution (§206 duty of care), MNPI /
  market-abuse surveillance (§204A; Exchange Act §10(b) / Rule 10b-5),
  the custody rule (17 CFR 275.206(4)-2), the marketing rule (17 CFR
  275.206(4)-1), cross-client allocation fairness / anti-cherry-picking
  (§206), books-and-records / off-channel-communications capture
  (17 CFR 275.204-2), and independent-valuation governance (§206 duty of
  loyalty). Includes a sub-vertical obligation map with
  primary-source-verified citations and a golden corpus of real public
  SEC enforcement actions wired as executable test fixtures. Zero runtime
  dependencies; property-tested; mypy --strict clean. Patterns were
  extracted from a multi-year private quantitative options research
  program (a separate program to which Marcos López de Prado is a named
  advisor on adjacent work; he is not an advisor to, contributor to, or
  endorser of this library) operating in paper-trading Phase 0 — no live
  capital has been deployed.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - autonomous agents
  - investment adviser
  - Advisers Act
  - fiduciary duty
  - private capital
  - regulated AI
  - human-in-the-loop
  - audit trail
  - compliance
